-- ============================================================================
-- seeds/warcastle-tables-6-10.sql
--
-- The real set-ups for WarCastle tables 6 to 10 (Grant's sketches, 4 Nov),
-- in the scenario builder's format, with no deployment (the attack sets
-- that) and no objective markers:
--   6 Mount Kalnas (snow): the altar (special feature), a dark stone
--     platform with steps on three sides and a ramp from the south up to a
--     level in the middle, and two scatter pieces.
--   7 Fortenhaf Town Centre (cobbles): a street from the west edge to
--     Fortenhaf Manor (special feature), low walls curving away from its
--     west end, five buildings and the ferry building.
--   8 Fortenhaf Market (cobbles): four buildings and two ruins.
--   9 Fortenhaf Gate: the town wall along the north with the Gates of
--     Fortenhaf on the road, and two hills.
--   10 Nagenhof Road: a road north to south, two woods, the Norman
--     Watchtower, the pub and two hills.
-- Terrain can still be moved in Set up > Tables.
--
-- Run in the Supabase SQL editor, after seeds/warcastle.sql. It sets
-- tables 6 to 10 and leaves the others as they are. Then re-run
-- seeds/warcastle-test.sql to copy them into WarCastle (test).
-- Safe to run again: the scenarios keep their ids.
-- ============================================================================

